  "rationale": "No single step is a single point of failure. The target is an OR of four collection steps, and several of them stay reachable through paths that share no intermediate step. (1) mailArchive:collection can be reached from phishing:initialAccess via browserStore:credentialAccess and fileServer:lateralMovement. It can also be reached via monitoringHost:lateralMovement, which depends on ssoLogin:authenticate (from workstation:execution and ciRunner:execution) or on vpnSession:authenticate. (2) codeRepo:collection can be reached via jumpHost:lateralMovement, which is fed by sshKey:credentialAccess, configSecret:credentialAccess or vpnSession:authenticate. It can also be reached via backupHost:lateralMovement, which is fed by configSecret:credentialAccess or kerberoast:credentialAccess. (3) shareMount:collection is reached via jumpHost:lateralMovement. Blocking any one non-foothold step leaves at least one complete path to crownData:exfiltrate. For example, blocking fileServer:lateralMovement still leaves the jumpHost:lateralMovement route to codeRepo:collection."
